    "body":  "## Summary\n\nFollow-up to merged #294 for two remaining OPFS read-visibility failures found by exact-head Browser-Only / Pages acceptance.\n\n- For confirmed Example replacement, retry the read-back of the newly published active `.vscode/settings.json`. A missing read is retried only while `stat` confirms the exact path remains a regular file. A genuinely missing path, changed file type, unavailable stat or non-missing I/O error still fails closed.\n- For the immutable dependency store, apply the same bounded, stat-confirmed retry to snapshot manifests and snapshot files. This covers transient `FileNotFound` / `EntryNotFound` after the snapshot directory has been published by rename; unresolved or genuinely missing snapshots remain `BLOCKED`, never READY.\n- Add fault-injection regressions for settings read-after-write and both filesystem missing-entry variants during snapshot verification.\n- Use the existing stat-confirmed retry helper when reading staged settings and the new bounded helper when verifying the published active settings.\n\nNo missing settings file or dependency snapshot is treated as success. Existing backup / rollback / recovery behavior and immutable snapshot digest verification remain intact.\n\n## Validation\n\nExact-head PR Verify, Native Windows, IDE Host, Theia Browser Host, Browser-Only Chromium and Pages Chromium are running / will rerun on the final head. The current-main failures are recorded in #280. #287 and #289 must be rerun after this fix is merged.\n\n## Tracking\n\nCloses #280\nPart of #279\n\nNo Runtime / 5GC / Production Qualification is claimed.",
